=== PRE-FLIGHT: does the S2 C-B variable define a branch population? ===
  C-B potential V = x.K_b.x/2 + beta sum x^4: min eig K_b = 0.3045 > 0, beta >= 0 => V strictly convex
  => unique equilibrium x = 0, no two attractors, no bounded [0,1] coordinate, no canonical map to |alpha|^2: UNFORMULABLE-FROM-S2

=== CORE: backward equation b h' + (1/2) sigma^2 h'' = 0, h(0)=0, h(1)=1 ===
  Born h(p) = p  =>  L p = b(p) * 1 + (1/2) sigma^2 * 0 = b(p)  =>  Born for all p in (0,1)  <=>  b == 0 on (0,1)
  scale function s'(p) = exp(-int 2b/sigma^2);  h(p) = s(p)/s(1) when s(0+), s(1-) finite and exit is a.s.

=== A: driftless Wright-Fisher-type, sigma^2 = 2 D p(1-p) ===
  h(p) = p exactly (s' = 1).  Mean absorption time E[tau] = -(p ln p + (1-p) ln(1-p))/D: solves D p(1-p) T'' = -1: True , T(0+), T(1-) = (0, 0)  (finite: exit boundaries, absorption in finite time)
  A': sigma = 4 sqrt(kappa) p(1-p) (QSD diffusive unraveling): speed density ~ 1/p^2 near 0 is non-integrable -> natural
      boundaries: absorption only ASYMPTOTIC (p_t -> {0,1} a.s. by bounded-martingale convergence), still h(p) = p

=== B: frozen nonlinear drift b = lam p(1-p)(2p-1), same sigma^2 = 2 D p(1-p); c = lam/D = 2 ===
  exact h_B(p): h(0.1)=0.07793, h(0.25)=0.21955, h(0.4)=0.38390, h(0.5)=0.50000, h(0.6)=0.61610, h(0.75)=0.78045, h(0.9)=0.92207
  h_B(p) - p   : -0.02207, -0.03045, -0.01610, +0.00000, +0.01610, +0.03045, +0.02207  -> SELECTION-NON-BORN (majority amplified)

