=== C: noise off (sigma = 0): p' = lam p(1-p)(2p-1) ===
  fixed points 0, 1/2 (unstable for lam>0), 1; p0>1/2 -> 1, p0<1/2 -> 0, approach exponential (asymptotic, never in finite time)
  'probability of branch 1' = mu({p0 > 1/2}) requires a SUPPLIED measure mu on initial conditions: DETERMINISTIC-BASINS / MEASURE-REQUIRED

=== D: noise without absorption: b = gamma(p0 - p), sigma^2 = 2 D p(1-p), gamma = 4, p0 = 1/2 ===
  stationary density ~ p^(2.0-1)(1-p)^(2.0-1) = Beta(2.0,2.0); exponents >= 1 => both boundaries unattainable
  MC from p0=0.25 to t=20: absorbed fraction 0.0290 (-> 0): NO-SELECTION (stochastic, fluctuating, no definite outcome)

=== E: same dephasing Lindblad (L = sqrt(kappa) sigma_z), two unravelings ===
  ensemble |rho_01|(t=4): random-unitary 0.0715, QSD 0.0635, Lindblad exact 0.0620
  populations: random-unitary p_t = 0.3 on every trajectory; QSD: mean 0.3013, fraction within 0.05 of 0 or 1: 0.907
  -> identical decoherence (same ensemble master equation); selection present only in the QSD unraveling

=== F: decomposition independence <=> Born (mixtures with the same rho_11) ===
  B: pure p=0.4 -> h=0.38390;  50/50 mixture of p=0.2, 0.6 (same rho_11 = 0.4) -> 0.39271: outcome frequencies depend on the decomposition
  A: h(p)=p -> both give 0.4. h decomposition-independent for all mixtures <=> h affine <=> (with h(0)=0, h(1)=1) h(p)=p
